cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  weave — an open-source, self-hosted, agent-accessible work platform
message: If you use weave in your work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Grunion AI
    website: https://github.com/grunion-ai
repository-code: https://github.com/grunion-ai/weave
abstract: >-
  weave is a portable work system you own, developed in the open. Connected
  records, documents and automations share one model. People use the browser;
  their existing agents use MCP, REST and CLI. The runtime uses Node.js and
  SQLite workspace storage, with zero runtime dependencies and no build step.
  MIT source, public tests and an open roadmap make development inspectable.
keywords:
  - work management
  - no-code database
  - self-hosted
  - local-first
  - Airtable alternative
  - Fibery alternative
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agents
  - SQLite
license: MIT
